{"reference":"Ezekiel 11","book":"Ezekiel","chapter":11,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"The Departure of Glory","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The vision’s final scene is often understood as part of a larger movement: the glory of YHWH leaves the defiled temple and city in Ezekiel 8–11, then returns to the visionary sanctuary in chapter 43. Here, the glory moves from the city to the mountain east of it, marking the close of Ezekiel’s vision before he is returned to the captives.","verse_refs":["Ezekiel 11:1-25"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_ezekiel_011_7c061cc41172116e2892c3dc"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}